On 1 Nov 2006 08:50:47 -0800, carlhnelson@gmail.com wrote:

>I generally have a lot of trouble keeping ponies/horses/warhorses alive
>because of the nutrition problem.  

  They'll eat food rations when hungry enough.  Just #chat to it every
so often to see if it's hungry.  It might even be possible to count
turns since it last ate a food ration and know when it will get hungry
again. 

  Wizmode testing:
  By turn 1012 a knight's starting horse was hungry:
   - "Whinnied" when chatted to
   - fed it an apple and #chatting go the "whickered" response

   By turn 1759 the horse was confused from hunger.
   Left the level and by turn 2000 the horse was feral.
     (Just a note, hostile horses "neigh".)
     - tossing a lizard corpse made the horse peaceful.
     - Throwing an apple to the horse retamed it (turn 2015).
     - The horse got hungry ("whinnie") about T:3205, 1190 turns later.
     - T:3709 horse is confused from hunger: ~1690 turns after taming.
     - T:3752 horse is still hungry, no longer confused despite not 
       eating.
     - T:3952 horse finally dies from starvation.


  Tamed horse took:
   - 1190 turns to get hungry, 
     - At this point horse's hitpoints are reduced to a percentage
       of max, presumably based on how hungry the horse is.
   - 1690 turns to start starving, 
     - Confusion from hunger wore off without eating
       - This has caused me to assume horse found something to eat 
         before.
   - 1937 turns to die from starvation.

  I've locked a tame warhorse into a room with a food ration while I was
busy in MineTown.  Checked the warhorse when the "feel worried" message
appeared and sure enough, he'd eaten the ration and was fine.

