  As horses are domesticated animals they don't have to be tamed
immediately.  Throwing them a tin, or even a meaty corpse (e.g. lizard),
will cause them to go peaceful.  Not only can this save your character's
life, it  "stores" the horse for you indefinitely.  It won't starve but
will always be there to tame.  

  For starving horses there's always the Stupid Pet Trick.  Leave the
pet on another level until it would have starved.  That will cause it to
go peaceful or hostile.  Then retame with some low nutrition item, like
a pear or apple.  (Maybe even a carrot if you've plenty to spare.)  This
may be the real purpose of a Knight's starting veggie rations.




